  "research_notes": "Research involved extensive cross-referencing of Texas state government directories and records. The primary sources were the Texas Comptroller’s official list of state agencies ([fmx.cpa.texas.gov](https://fmx.cpa.texas.gov/fm/contacts/agynum/index.php#:~:text=458%20%20,Texas%20Board%20of%20Architectural%20Examiners)) ([fmx.cpa.texas.gov](https://fmx.cpa.texas.gov/fm/contacts/agynum/index.php#:~:text=match%20at%20L123%20529%20,Board%20of%20Occupational%20Therapy%20Examiners)) and the Texas State Library’s agency directory, supplemented by the Wikipedia compilation of Texas state agencies ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Texas_state_agencies#:~:text=,Texas%20Legislative%20Reference%20Library)) ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Texas_state_agencies#:~:text=,73)). This ensured coverage of all branches: legislative (e.g., Texas Senate, House, Legislative agencies), judicial (courts and related offices), and executive agencies (departments, commissions, boards, etc.). Additional entities such as state retirement systems and interstate compacts (e.g., Texas Emergency Services Retirement System ([fmx.cpa.texas.gov](https://fmx.cpa.texas.gov/fm/contacts/agynum/index.php#:~:text=323%20%20,Veterans%20Land%20Board)) and the Low-Level Radioactive Waste Disposal Compact Commission) were included for completeness. The final list includes over 160 legal entities associated with the State of Texas, ranging from major departments to smaller boards and councils. All names were verified against official sources to use exact legal designations. This comprehensive list is believed to be complete as of the latest available records; any recently created entities (such as the Texas Permanent School Fund Corporation ([fmx.cpa.texas.gov](https://fmx.cpa.texas.gov/fm/contacts/agynum/index.php#:~:text=696%20%20,%E2%80%93%20Office%20of%20Technology%20Commercialization)) and the Fifteenth Court of Appeals) are included. One limitation is that extremely temporary committees (e.g., one-time inaugural committees) were not included, focusing instead on established and statutory entities. Overall, confidence in the completeness of this list is high, given the multiple authoritative references used and the broad scope of the search.",
